cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this ontology, please cite it as below. This project is an integral part
  of the doctoral research of Jefferson Rodrigo Speck in the Graduate Program in
  Informatics (PPGInf) of the Federal University of Paraná (UFPR), supervised by
  Prof. Dr. Roberto Pereira (UFPR) and co-supervised by Prof. Dr. Clodis Boscarioli
  (UNIOESTE). No DOI has been assigned yet.
title: "Artistic Reality Ontology (ARO)"
version: 0.2.0-beta
date-released: 2026-10-30
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Speck
    given-names: Jefferson Rodrigo
    affiliation: "Universidade Federal do Paraná (UFPR), Programa de Pós-Graduação em Informática (PPGInf)"
abstract: >-
  Ontology (OWL, SHACL, SKOS) for representing artworks in any medium, plural
  interpretations of their passages, represented situations and patterns, contestable
  claims of correspondence with documented real cases, and derivation between works.
  Developed with the SABiOx methodology and grounded in UFO.
  Doctoral project, Graduate Program in Informatics (PPGInf), Federal University of
  Paraná (UFPR). Supervisor: Prof. Dr. Roberto Pereira (UFPR). Co-supervisor:
  Prof. Dr. Clodis Boscarioli (UNIOESTE). Linked to the Research Group on Technology
  and Innovation in Education (GTIE), Western Paraná State University (UNIOESTE).
keywords:
  - ontology
  - OntoUML
  - UFO
  - SABiOx
  - art and reality
  - interpretation
  - derivation
  - knowledge representation
